<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
    The hardened runtime, which notarization requires, turns on library
    validation: every library loaded into the process must carry the same
    Team ID as the executable.  A PyInstaller one-file binary unpacks
    its bundled libraries (``libpython3.14.dylib`` and friends) to a
    temporary directory at startup and loads them from there, and those
    copies keep the ad-hoc signature PyInstaller gave them.  Without this
    exception the binary dies immediately with "mapping process and mapped
    file (non-platform) have different Team IDs".

    Signing the unpacked libraries is not an option: they only exist once
    the binary has already started.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
